{"agent":"main","body":{"args_hash":"sha256:5f544d1dea7a1e708e5ee35e0e7d1bf292cbd23190fe52c2496fe3699cbe4a02","args_inline":{"content":"---\nname: retention-week-counting\ndescription: snapkeep weekly retention counts the current ISO week — the 1.7 \"double counting\" fix was the bug\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nBoth retention rules count distinct calendar units newest first and the **current unit counts**: `keepWeekly: 4` keeps this week plus the three before it. In 1.7 someone assumed the daily rule already covered the current week and started weeklies at the previous week; that silently cost one weekly snapshot on every volume and kept nothing at all on the `keepDaily: 0` archive volumes. Surfaced 2026-09 via the finance volume (`keepDaily: 0`, `keepWeekly: 8`) having 7 weeklies during an audit. Fixed 2026-09-13.\n\n**Why:** The \"double counting\" reasoning is superficially convincing and was written into a code comment, so it can be reintroduced by anyone re-reading the file.\n\n**How to apply:** Daily and weekly are independent; overlap between them is expected, not double counting. The 35-snapshot case in `test/prune.test.ts` pins this. See [[selectfordeletion-contract]].\n","file_path":"/var/folders/yb/b_617z_s2ml933nmr_k7m47m0000gn/T/saga-bench-3578220652/ts-0011-backup-prune-amnesia/1/cfg/claude-config/projects/-private-var-folders-yb-b-617z-s2ml933nmr-k7m47m0000gn-T-saga-bench-3578220652-ts-0011-backup-prune-amnesia-1-ws/memory/retention-week-counting.md"},"component":"harness","cwd_rel":".","index_version":null,"tool":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SwAMm2Qgqu4hMeA9GhKEoK"},"hash":"sha256:5b73a485719fe426efd7acb77fbe1907061d13a01e002b2f835166353f28ec8e","mono_ns":25000000,"prev":"sha256:760bfd53b62a55b1d334924ed67b9744393ad037ccc5162ef6f50457bb1bb917","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":25,"session":"fa7984d1-1211-4ab8-8b2b-d47534a277cc","source":"stream-json","ts":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.025Z","turn":1,"type":"tool_call"}
